{"title":"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_grogg007\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by grogg007</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_-_Trinomial_Factorization_for_solutions_by_HungryCalculator\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution - Trinomial Factorization for solutions by HungryCalculator</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_yjtest\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by yjtest</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />, where both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are integers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060d8850e65d5781ce12d9fe2681f401dd6ee77c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a535646f69c9dc4230d60aca3118a2a563a884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x^2-xy-6y^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_grogg007\">Video solution by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by grogg007\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PNBxBvvjbcU?t=401\">https://youtu.be/PNBxBvvjbcU?t=401</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by factoring, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd746f962390837f58027d9581d02c0570b934d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x^2-xy-6y^2=(3x+2y)(4x-3y)=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"340\" height=\"21\" /> Since the RHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we have two options,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebf5a86e7725db1ac3fa3396ed38c1797735583f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{\\text{Case 1:}}\\text{ } 3x+2y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>In this case we have, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6db0167f464a4c8c6093a6886c55f3e685cc80e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{-3x}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" /> Using the bounding on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> we have, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de8e49d1c17e94ca2735d3486c3855ee7bb3584.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-100\\le\\frac{-3x}{2}\\le 100.\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"37\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f9814fd6808dd49986a82a14712fc8c68c9b8714.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{200}{3}\\ge x \\ge \\frac{-200}{3}.\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"37\" />\nIn addition in order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b1aa56353a0f98d2916ff8c14c263c19666bdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 | x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> so we substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bbc4cd67de64297483f3192fd287f075eed0b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2k.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/f/04f48d578d7709db147a9eefb8ef2c6c7ce8e57d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{200}{3}\\ge 2k \\ge \\frac{-200}{3}.\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/602c8bcb0400f3f4e9071f39b85f5b6af042ef56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{100}{3}\\ge k \\ge \\frac{-100}{3}.\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"37\" /> From this we have solutions starting from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a5932903d1d3f180856eb7710d6f2fc4ea5a038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-33$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa7247f4d29d95459cbf6f238007a1b1090ebea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$67$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> solutions.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/742c440e98213afdb975417a5fb01915aa091a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{\\text{Case 2: }}\\text{ } 4x-3y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>On the other hand, we have, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24f1921dd351e28e624ec26011536f94a2015386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{4x}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" /> From bounds we have, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45cb83df7a7916b2fd2e1d42642833ba1d114d87.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-100\\le\\frac{4x}{3}\\le 100.\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"37\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/e/a0e45bc4f5e31edf7e172b92453ffaae963639d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-75 \\le x \\le 75.\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"15\" />\nIn this case, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41f9e29f722e70e381f947c708cec388d36ff128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 | x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> so we substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/e/72e9a697239fae889ef54a65678f201254c89ff0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3t.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/19044a3f6dd07a154ff4d25fba15748c325cd5fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-75 \\le 3t \\le 75.\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5dbf68c0a6b7cbdfbc845d446844d2954744d4af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-25 \\le t \\le 25.\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> solutions.\n</p><p>Finally we overcount one case which is the intersection of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lines (which are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/512919ab7241a0a58b5b23042200377e8b21f6f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{-3x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/35028056e2e40da91f0e89298caa386f2edfe856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{4x}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />) or the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff5ce595f91c217539cd5e3a6239b0abcf47265.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> Therefore our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a50c6dc17071e7c202525077e86c41274902692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$67+51-1=\\boxed{117}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Mathkiddus\" title=\"User:Mathkiddus\">mathkiddus</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If one can't factor the quadratic or is looking for an easier way than guess and check:\n</p><p>First, remove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> entirely and assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/0/ea0c648440c3fe1aa42ac8277e36d9ff24758c2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x^2 - x-6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />. This factors to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db58e9d722eb8f4bf76e5ea8a50dec295a008f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3x+2)(4x-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />. Now, just append <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> at the end and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a69b72041267a4cae422a31fb754db79baf8a432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3x+2y)(4x-3y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />. Good as new!\n</p><p>For those who don't understand how this works, it is through the properties of <b>homogeneous quadratics</b>. We want to keep 0, so we split the middle term to two numbers such that they multiply to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87bb13dbd5457e104467ea0ac334a0c2c3b8d587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\cdot (-6) = -72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" /> and add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. Those terms are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a483ee25b066703890405f0127fef9c31572fb81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we split the middle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> term as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/994f0742f20fc800e5c5c9dbfd540fa7cab6db47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x^2 - 9xy + 8xy - 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />, and we factor out into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/413f9857811e88862a9fa1a2bc1ec7447921f8f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x(4x - 3y) - 2y(4x-3y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" />, and thus into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d2f780a70760592084188fee8c786979288e84f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3x-2y)(4x-3y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is a solution.\n</p><p>Divide the equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5a3faa3658bcbd8bde8e16cfa5baf019619fc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" />, getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b431b024ce26ef1b4f26c32cc7964acf71d00c41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12(\\frac{x}{y})^2-\\frac{x}{y}-6 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"157\" height=\"38\" />. (We can ignore the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> case for now.) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842c7273008239c636c25856b7df08504709e043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />. We now have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77ead08c2c59d7a8589107f28cbdea8df3743cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12a^2-a-6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />. Factoring, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/5/575f1e106f57216dd45b38e1700e6bcd8fbf15bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4a-3)(3a+2) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, the graph is satisfied when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8fe5f2b40ec2161cf087f832c6db63722072400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529f1b2f2e0e7866b2f9dc46d026d7f80c05fbb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a=-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/642ab04938a0f6d4961d63fb1449990b42f3e9d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y} = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> back into the equations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a4032465f4dd364a1eac1411ae0987760a35ec83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x=3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/b/f5b2b336eb417bdd8fad6b5affc22966f5a72716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x=-2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Remember that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060d8850e65d5781ce12d9fe2681f401dd6ee77c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, inclusive. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a4032465f4dd364a1eac1411ae0987760a35ec83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x=3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />, the solutions are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93135c5b202fbac8e112f7a54d869d55d2d3ee2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-75,-100), (-72,-96), (-69, -92), \\dots, (72,96), (75,100)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"462\" height=\"20\" />. Remember to not count the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08cc55a3a19c9f8cf005f17391db8ed355d2909c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> case for now. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> positive solutions and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> negative solutions for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919cbf14fcd215b2bc2efc0935d81ed4a38e4cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x-2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />, we do something similar. The solutions are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31bfc5336f207bcaefb8976b393eb0f436e08725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-66,99), (-64,96), \\dots, (64, -96), (66, -99)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"349\" height=\"20\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> solutions when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is positive and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> solutions when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is negative, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now we can count the edge case of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. The answer is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b9c40f4285adf9d50fdc227c31a7617a7427047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50+66+1 = \\boxed{117}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>P.S. This technique of dividing by y^2 and then substituting a variable for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" /> is called de-homogeneization.\n~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can use the quadratic formula for this equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/82650dd56b4082fd5508712e6152c81fd2771fa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x^2 - xy - 6y^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />;\nAlthough this solution may seem to be misleading, it works! What we are doing is considering the quadratic with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/991e880218e5e3ab98bee23a95c133b391f034bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> is the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c716d1dc907ae6b51cb0f545664c89d58b6b67d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/347180320df25dae18ce8a189e7566986f76b26f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> is the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b033ca765f3147195d02e868207975548bcfe24e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is the constant term.\n</p><p>You get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b2320d42a7395a92a186b7655c6afa97a2f08b70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46de5554f2c749d7450e459dcabff72c69bd3a94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{xy \\pm \\sqrt{x^2 y^2 + (12\\cdot6\\cdot4\\cdot x^2 \\cdot y^2)}}{24x^2}\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604c81ee7beabbddb7957711ac258c1d7344edb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{xy \\pm\\sqrt{289x^2 y^2}}{24x^2}\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d552c2596fd6b117043088d7c07af048d3ad86f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{18xy}{24x^2}\\text{, and }\\frac{-16xy}{24x^2}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Rather than putting this equation as zero, the numerators and denominators must be equal [EDIT: We set each value equal to one because the quadratic is taken with respect to the root <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />]. These two equations simplify to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2ae0b82d13ca79b94064a0bf7f3f07ff08310a95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3y = 4x;\\]\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5ca971d0c5a2fa253b59a072185bb2ac3b2a0425.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-2y = 3x;\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060d8850e65d5781ce12d9fe2681f401dd6ee77c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, for the first equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9a4137107169bd5b85dd91cf817535ddbf3775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-75,75]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f823254edeced5425c35898b6b80b8f907fb38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((75+75)/3) + 1 = 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" /> solutions for this case.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/034b4adce82f539b8afb8e0ee5a4ad791299d164.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-2y = 3x:\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29e113f126cef6be9008708f2699605e2c7d6a84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-66, 66]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has to be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73d720abc33124f2384dbe029df4ce11d674cdf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(66+66)/2 + 1 = 67$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> solutions for this case.\n</p><p>However, the one overlap would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, because y would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in both solutions.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bcaf4cd7c50cdd58883a72f729eb75e3a459ab89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51+67-1 = \\boxed{117}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"160\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p><br />\n-U-King3.14Root\n-LaTeX corrected by Andrew2019\n-clarified by golden_star_123\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J-0BapU4Yuk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J-0BapU4Yuk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_-_Trinomial_Factorization_for_solutions_by_HungryCalculator\">Video Solution - Trinomial Factorization for solutions by HungryCalculator</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution - Trinomial Factorization for solutions by HungryCalculator\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BL42BudtUOE&amp;t\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BL42BudtUOE&amp;t</a>\n</p><p>~HungryCalculator\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_yjtest\">Video Solution by yjtest</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by yjtest\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P7LEfKK1Vew\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P7LEfKK1Vew</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I\" title=\"2025 AIME I\">2025 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018030830\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 662/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20086/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.705      1 -total\n 57.77%    7.340      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.56%    5.026      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:29723:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018030830 and revision id 285677. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}